<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brecon Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1093</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brecon Castle is a Norman castle at Brecon in mid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernard-de-neufmarche">Bernard de Neufmarché</a> after his conquest of the Welsh kingdom of Brycheiniog around 1093. It was the centre of the marcher lordship of Brecknock, held in turn by the de Braose, de Bohun and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stafford">Stafford</a> families. Parts of the great hall and towers survive, partly incorporated into a hotel.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brecon-castle.jpg" alt="Brecon Castle" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Philip Pankhurst · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brecon_Castle_(geograph_4250259).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
